== Exercise 4.2: weighted class scheduling
OK   4.2 [0,3] (2 credits) + [1,2] (1 credit): rule EF earns 1 on every run, optimum 2
OK   4.2 [0,3] (2 credits) + [1,2] (1 credit): rule c earns 1 on every run, optimum 2
OK   4.2 [0,3] (2 credits) + [1,2] (1 credit): rule h earns 1 on every run, optimum 2
OK   4.2 [0,3] (2 credits) + [1,2] (1 credit): rule i earns 1 on every run, optimum 2
OK   4.2(b) with 1 credit per class the credit of a schedule is its size (so 4.1's counterexamples carry over)
OK   4.2(c) MaxCredit DP equals brute force (all class sets over 0..5 up to 4 classes, random up to 9)  [14820 weighted inputs]
